The original proof of concept worked, but it still carried several experimental pieces. This cleaned version:

removes the unused radius argument, the unfinished rotation method, debug prints, commented experiments, and the incomplete coordinate setter;
corrects symetric to axisymmetric and uses camelCase throughout the wrapper;
exposes planar depth and the mesh minimum angle as separate settings;
replaces the hard-coded blah.fem output with a required file path;
records created materials and circuits;
turns coils into ordinary blocks with circuit properties instead of maintaining a disconnected Coil class;
adds validation for shapes and coordinate counts;
supports nonlinear B-H points directly on a material; and
clears FEMM selections after post-processing so one query cannot silently affect the next.

The official pyFEMM reference manual is still the source of truth for problem definitions, material parameters, boundary conditions, and block-integral type numbers. This wrapper is deliberately thin, so any missing FEMM feature can still be called directly through femm.



